      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. so you're saying the media basically validates one group's motives while criminalizing the other's based on race. do you think there's any specific way the wording changes regarding the \"threat level\"? like, would they describe the suburbanites as \"concerned citizens\" even if they're being aggressive, versus describing the city group as a \"threat to public safety\" or something similar? i'm trying to see if the \"danger\" aspect is tied specifically to the race of the protesters in these media models.",
