      "content": "Yes, the media often employs a dual standard where \"concerned citizens\" or \"taxpayers\" are used to describe white suburbanites, framing their tactics as legitimate civic engagement even when aggressive. In contrast, similar actions by marginalized groups are frequently labeled as a \"breaking of the law\" or a \"public safety threat,\" emphasizing violence and chaos rather than political intent. This linguistic shift effectively decouples the actions from the protesters' personhood when they are white, but reifies a stereotype of inherent danger when they are Black, blame-racing the entirety of the act onto the demographic rather than the specific tactics used. Ultimately, this selective violence framing reinforces a hierarchical narrative that viewerly the safety of the majority while eroding the legitimacy of the minority's grievance.",
